WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.960
Every truck journey creates information.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.760
Keeping it connected is the challenge.

3
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.460
Northstar brings drivers, dispatch and
accounting into one shared workflow.

4
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.700
The rota gives each driver a truck, a
destination and a working schedule.

5
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.720
In the driver workspace, they can review
the assignment, start their shift and

6
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.620
begin the journey.

7
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.800
Dispatch follows the fleet on a UK map
with journey progress, driver details

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.920
and estimated arrival times.

9
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.800
Reported stops and recorded notes help the
dispatcher understand what needs

10
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.000
attention.

11
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.380
When a truck reaches its destination,

12
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.020
Northstar records the arrival and saves
the journey report.

13
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.820
Then n8n picks up the event.

14
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.980
It retrieves the journey details, sends
the owner an arrival notification

15
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.200
and prepares an AI accounting summary from
the recorded figures.

16
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.360
Fuel, driver and vehicle costs are
presented as estimates with assumptions

17
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.820
and missing information clearly
identified.

18
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.420
The summary returns to Northstar.

19
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.800
An accounting email is sent and Google
Sheets becomes a searchable journey

20
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.360
register.

21
00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.460
Saved summaries, email receipts and event
progress help avoid repeating

22
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.300
completed work.

23
00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.820
Built as a working portfolio MVP,

24
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.620
Northstar uses simulated fleet movement
and fictional cost assumptions.

25
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:25.120
One connected journey, from the driver's
first action to the accounting team's

26
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:25.860
final report.

27
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.560
Mark Automates, a little less admin, a lot
more you.
